event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":0,"content_block":{"type":"compaction","content":"MISSION SUMMARY (carry-on notes for Claudia Kermin)\n\nMISSION ID AND GOAL\n- Mission m20261101-160346-2997.\n- Mission Goal, in the player's words (quoted): \"Fly to Duna and land anywhere\"\n- Crewed Mission: Claudia flies aboard. Crew seats: 1; free: 0; no other Kerbals aboard. If Claudia is killed, the Mission is Lost.\n- Mission type: crewed. Game mode: SANDBOX. Craft name \"Mun Shot\", vessel_id cf4cb7019e9c44588f838d76597263c8.\n- Spending Cap: $10.00.\n\nMISSION SETTINGS (verbatim)\n- Daylight landing: on. Set the land block's daylight option to true and prefer a daylight landing.\n- Time versus delta-v, Balanced: wait up to 6 h to save delta-v; do not wait longer than that for a better window.\n- Physics warp on Coasts: on. Blocks warp through Coasts with physics warp where rails can't; use the warp helpers for your own Coasts.\n- Asked in chat to stop or allow physics warp, point the player to that setting; change no plan until they switch it.\n\nPLAYER INSTRUCTIONS (as the player said them)\n1. Mission Goal: \"Fly to Duna and land anywhere\".\n2. Change request (quoted): \"Add a step to extend solar panels after launch\". It was done: the Mission Plan was revised and the step flown.\n3. The player approved the Mission Plan and each Sequence Plan so far.\n- Auto Mode is on: plans are pre-approved, so don't ask the player questions. State assumptions and give a brief reason for each decision.\n- Blackout is active (link false). The player can't see or answer until the link returns. The mod runs Sequence Plans and takes revised Mission Plans without asking. Revisions must stay within the Mission Goal and the Spending Cap, and the player reads every revision's why when the link returns. A Failed Debrief makes the craft safe and waits; never end the Mission or reduce the goal myself.\n\nAPPROVED MISSION PLAN (revised, with the solar panel step)\nTotal delta-v 6085 m/s, expected duration \"About 1.5 to 2 Kerbin years including the window wait\", mission_time_s 20000000, no child vessels. Goal steps: 1 Reach Kerbin orbit; 2 Extend solar panels; 3 Transfer to Duna; 4 Capture into Duna orbit; 5 Land on Duna.\n1. \"Launch to Kerbin orbit\". Intent: Launch and circularize in an 80 km orbit. 3385 m/s. Timing: Immediately.\n2. \"Extend solar panels\". Intent: Extend the solar panels in orbit with a short custom script and check that charge is rising. 0 m/s. Timing: Right after orbit is reached.\n3. \"Duna transfer\". Intent: Wait for the Duna window, eject, and trim the course for a Duna periapsis of about 100 km. 1150 m/s. Timing: Wait for the Kerbin-Duna window, then about 300 days of coast.\n4. \"Duna capture\". Intent: Capture into a low circular Duna orbit. 650 m/s. Timing: On arrival at Duna.\n5. \"Duna landing\". Intent: Deorbit and land on Duna with a powered descent in daylight, using the remaining stage, legs and parachute. 900 m/s. Timing: After capture, waiting up to 6 h for daylight.\n\nFLOWN SEQUENCES AND DEBRIEFS\n- Step 1, Launch to Kerbin orbit: Nominal.\n  - Script: launch(target_ap 80000, turn_shape 0.55, stage_limit 2), then circularize at ap with stage_limit 2.\n  - Result: orbit 79690 by 79580 m, inc 0.11, ecc 8e-5, dv_used 3567 m/s from stock (the script reported 19.8 for the circularize).\n  - Staging events: stages 7, 6, 5 and 4 fired.\n- Step 2, Extend solar panels: Nominal.\n  - Custom script removed stale nodes, extended 4 panels, and EC rose from 889 to 907.\n- Step 3, Duna transfer. Flown as several Sequence Plans, all with plan_step 3:\n  a) Ejection burn (custom script computing a phase angle, and the ejection point and dv by formula): script success, node 1072.5 m/s, used 1089 m/s, residual 0.08, window UT 11490849. Debrief Nominal. The resulting orbit was an escape from Kerbin, but a Minmus encounter (Minmus pe 1429 km) followed and cut the Sun orbit to ap 16.86 million km by pe 12.83 million km. That is short of Duna's 20.7 million km. The window phase calculation was wrong by about 114 degrees: Duna was about 70 degrees behind Kerbin instead of 44 degrees ahead.\n  b) Coast out of Kerbin SOI to UT 11570900: Nominal, now in a Sun orbit.\n  c) Direct Lambert (solve_burn intercept_at) tests at several departure times and flight times cost 3400 to 10600 m/s, so they were rejected.\n  d) Phasing burn at the Sun periapsis (UT 12576930): Nominal, used 324 m/s, Sun orbit became ap 19.70 million km altitude by pe 12.83 million km altitude, period 12.33 million s.\n  e) Duna intercept burn at UT 37233510 (node radial 13.33, normal -31.65, prograde -30.11, from solve_burn intercept_at, tof 6.0 million s): Nominal, used 43.6 m/s, next patch Duna.\n  f) Mid-course \"Duna mid-course and approach\" (tune_pe next, value 100000, tolerance 20000): refused by the mod, Off-Nominal. The periapsis reached was -15 km (over tolerance), after a 0.1 m/s burn.\n  g) \"Duna mid-course retry\" (value 110000, tolerance 40000): refused, Off-Nominal. The periapsis reached was 38 km, with a 0.2 m/s burn.\n  h) \"Duna late mid-course\" (coast to 150000 s before the SOI change, then tune_pe next, value 110000, tolerance 40000, then coast to encounter+60): Nominal.\n     - Zero dv was needed; the periapsis had drifted to 94.2 km.\n     - The craft is now inside the Duna SOI.\n- Delta-v left now: 3007.1 m/s. The mod's margin recheck: 3007 m/s against 1550 m/s still to fly (enough).\n\nCURRENT CRAFT STATE (latest Game Snapshot, UT 43185490.7; parts unchanged since UT 11490953.93, 37 parts)\n- Situation ESCAPING (hyperbolic), body Duna. Altitude 47541188.7 m, vertical speed -1014.04 m/s. Lat -0.44, celestial longitude 226.55.\n- Orbit around Duna:\n  - pe 94224.2 m, ap -1327530 (hyperbolic), ecc 2.3963, inc 152.208 (retrograde).\n  - lan 225.713, arg_pe 112.948, sma -296652.7.\n- Craft mass 8.7917 t, stage 4 (the current stage number).\n- Stages:\n  - stage 3: dv_vac 777.66, TWR 2.32 at Duna, burn time 101.8 s, mass 8792 to 6986 kg.\n  - stage 2: dv_vac 2229.39, TWR 3.28, burn time 169.2 s, mass 6216 to 3216 kg.\n  - stages 1 and 0: 1415 kg, no thrust.\n  - Total dv 3007.1 m/s, thrust 60 kN (the Terrier).\n- Resources:\n  - ElectricCharge 1055/1055.\n  - MonoPropellant 126.59/130.\n  - Ablator 199.97/200.\n  - LiquidFuel 432.48/630.\n  - Oxidizer 528.59/770.\n- Commnet link false (blackout). A stale past node may sit in the node list; scripts remove all nodes first.\n- Crew: Claudia Kermin (SuperIntelligence). Experiment: crewReport (science_left null).\n- Parts (37), as of the UT 11490953.93 snapshot. The format is id, name, stage, key facts:\n  - 2728776223 mk1pod.v2 (Mk1 Command Pod), stage -1, 1 seat, tags crew_seat, command, reaction_wheel, experiment, antenna, aero_stabiliser, EC 50.\n  - 1610885350 parachuteSingle (Mk16), stage 0, parent of the pod.\n  - 2946601144 longAntenna (Communotron 16), stage 0.\n  - 211703328 kOSMachine1m (kOS processor), stage -1.\n  - 3337518356 batteryBank (EC 1000), stage -1.\n  - 3010912453 HeatShield1 (1.25 m, also a decoupler, ablator), stage -1.\n  - 2796149853 Decoupler.1 (TD-12), stage 1, under the heat shield. Firing stage 1 would separate the pod from the rest of the stack, so never stage below 2.\n  - 2825157257 RCSFuelTank (FL-R120), stage 1, with 4 RV-1X RCS blocks (843541563, 2030726344, 3148022542, 352078390).\n  - 1970914001 fuelTank (FL-T400), stage 1.\n  - 1827728043 fuelTankSmall (FL-T200), stage 1, with 4 landing legs LT-1 (2566587550, 1106004823, 2026665805, 2954950894), stage 1.\n  - 2561074321 liquidEngine3.v2 (LV-909 Terrier, 60 kN vac, Isp 345), stage 3.\n  - Two radial decouplers on the FL-T400 at stage 2: 394153501 and 1156497556. Each carries an FL-T400 tank (1342040560, 2175741820) with 2 nose cones each (2171697554, 3506301837, 4089622760, 2099367185) and a fuel line (2268116198, 3662067021).\n  - 4 SP-L solar panels (solarPanels2: 890102882, 2466365216, 4092469140, 3673692998), stage 1, now extended.\n  - 4 RV-1X RCS blocks on the FL-T400 (2779650729, 4248169318, 2931699706, 1042241426), stage 1.\n  - All launch boosters, the Swivel and the Reliants, the old side tanks and the winglets and fins have been dropped. Stage 3's two radial tanks (1229234303, 1648233526, 786698223, 847630932, 1550082442, 1436298998, 4248147569, 2641128584, 1468394517, 12128237) were dropped during the ejection burn.\n\nPENDING SEQUENCE PLAN (just sent, awaiting approval)\n- plan_step 4, \"Duna capture\". Circularize at periapsis in a low Duna orbit, about 723 m/s, expected duration 55000 s.\n- Script:\n  local stale is allnodes.\n  for nd in stale { remove nd. }\n  local res is circularize(lexicon(\"at\", \"pe\", \"stage_limit\", 2, \"tolerance\", 0.02)).\n  addons:claudia:report(res).\n- Tolerances: eccentricity under 0.02, periapsis above 60 km. Telemetry checks: periapsis below 60000, delta_v_used above 900, EC below 15 percent.\n\nSEQUENCES STILL TO FLY\n- Step 4 (Duna capture), pending approval.\n- Step 5 (Duna landing), about 900 m/s budgeted.\n  - Duna has an atmosphere (50 km, 0.0667 atm) and surface gravity 2.943 m/s². The land block is for airless bodies only.\n  - Use a custom script for deorbit and a powered descent, with the parachute (stage 0, one Mk16), legs (stage 1) and the Terrier.\n  - Do not fire stage 1 (its decoupler separates the pod), and take care that staging does not drop the heat-shield stack unintentionally.\n  - Use the daylight setting and wait up to 6 h at most.\n  - Consider the heat shield and reentry or deorbit blocks (they support Duna), and check Duna surface TWR with stage_performance.\n\nLESSONS FROM FAILED OR OFF-NOMINAL ATTEMPTS\n- Phase-angle estimation from kOS positionat and body positions gave a window about 114 degrees off. For future interplanetary planning, verify geometry with solve_burn intercept_at and predict_burn, not just my own approximation.\n- Minmus flyby after the ejection cost the heliocentric speed, which led to the phasing burn plan.\n- solve_burn intercept_at returns dv in node components. In a script use node(ut, radial, normal, prograde), which is the kOS order. Burn at the Sun periapsis for cheap raising.\n- solve_burn set_ap burns only at the periapsis (do not pass \"at\"). solve_burn next_patch_pe threw an ArgumentException when called in the Sun orbit.\n- Maneuver node components are quantized at about 0.03 m/s (1/32). Early mid-course tunes therefore moved the periapsis by about 47 km per step. Tune late (150000 s before the SOI change) for fine control. tune_pe patch \"next\" always burns at the start of the remaining coast.\n- Keep stage_limit at 2 in every script so staging never fires stage 1.\n- The mod removes no stale nodes, so scripts should remove allnodes at the start.\n- Do not call propose_mission_plan unless the request asks for a Mission Plan.","signature":""}  }

